 theory and historical music trends in 2020 but found those approaches tedious and overwhelming. They have expressed interest in engaging with music through genres, cultural significance, live performances, album artwork, lyrics, and themed playlists. They launched a podcast discussing the fusion of traditional and electronic music, and enrolled in an audio production workshop after attending a hands-on workshop. They also experienced a stifling collaborative band situation, leading to a desire for more autonomy. They explored audio production techniques but found them unfulfilling, preferring to focus on creating their own tracks. They played board games but found them unengaging. They have realized the importance of focusing on what truly inspires them.\",\"version\":2,\"source_ids\":[\"s24\",\"s15\",\"s4\",\"s89\",\"s5\",\"s61\",\"s91\",\"s82\",\"s90\",\"s110\",\"s6\",\"s54\",\"s64\",\"s62\",\"s52\",\"s80\",\"s111\",\"s100\",\"s53\",\"s25\",\"s63\",\"s99\",\"s7\",\"s51\",\"s3\",\"s16\",\"s27\",\"s23\",\"s107\",\"s81\",\"s26\",\"s109\",\"s108\"],\"demand\":\"creative_history\",\"type\":\"text\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"}},\"getaway_prefs\":{\"value\":\"The user values creatively fulfilling weekend getaways that allow for hands-on, practical engagement with music and sound. They prefer unstructured exploration over rigid curricula, and enjoy attending live performances, discovering album artwork/lyrics/stories, making themed playlists, and connecting music to personal life. They are enrolled in an audio production workshop to deepen technical skills in mixing and mastering, and are committed to original composition over remixing. They dislike overly analytical or theoretical approaches that feel tedious or overwhelming, and prefer activities that foster emotional connection and personal expression.\",\"version\":1,\"source_ids\":[\"s35\",\"s24\",\"s36\",\"s4\",\"s5\",\"s61\",\"s6\",\"s45\",\"s64\",\"s44\",\"s62\",\"s25\",\"s63\",\